ong tone (communication/cooperation). So strong reliability and stress, but communication issues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), difficulty communicating ideas (cooperation), regarded as egocentric (cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). Positive: puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation), excellent attention skills (attention). Mixed.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but considered moody, regarded as a loner (cooperation). So strong technical, responsibility, but cooperation issues.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues. Candidate A has leadership but unfriendly. Candidate D has responsibility but moody/loner. Candidate C has decision quality and concern for others but egocentric and poor communication.\n\nWhich candidate has the best balance? Perhaps Candidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, good technical (weather, computer). Communication issues are a concern but maybe can be mitigated. Candidate A's unfriendly may be more severe for crew cooperation. Candidate D's moody/loner also problematic. Candidate C's egocentric and unwillingness to learn is concerning.\n\nThus I would recommend Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference discussion (none) but can say \"Given the criteria and the facts we have, I propose...\". Provide evidence: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, but note pretentiousness and tone issues.\n\nOk produce output."}
